From 98695cd525fe23361cb5af7fbe78084e1ee2ffc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:56:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 53/54] ARM: dts: omap3-n950: SGX530 at CORE/2

The PowerVR SGX530 ran from the reset default CORE/3, 130 MHz with the
N950's 390 MHz CORE clock. Harmattan runs it at CORE/2, 195.2 MHz (read on
an N9; its driver asks for up to 200 MHz, fclock_max in
board-rm680-video.c). Ask for that rate on the SGX functional clock; its
mux picks CORE/2. (sgx_mux_fck itself is only a component of the
composite sgx_fck and cannot be named in assigned-clocks: the module's
probe was deferred for good and the GPU had no driver.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap3-n950.dts | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap3-n950.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap3-n950.dts
index 7a905875d..91ef46b2c 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap3-n950.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap3-n950.dts
@@ -729,3 +729,13 @@ fm_codec_dai: simple-audio-card,codec {
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * PowerVR SGX530 at CORE/2 (195 MHz with the 390 MHz CORE clock) instead of
+ * the reset default CORE/3 (130 MHz): Harmattan's driver ran it at up to
+ * 200 MHz on this board (fclock_max in board-rm680-video.c).
+ */
+&sgx_module {
+	assigned-clocks = <&sgx_fck>;
+	assigned-clock-rates = <195200000>;
+};
-- 
